WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.210
Casting a key role can be critical to a film's
success, particularly when it comes to characters

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.570
that have been deeply explored before.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:12.110
Unfortunately, in the cases of these films
and TV features, the casting decisions were

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.100
downright awful.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.300
The first look at Joseph Fiennes in the role
of Michael Jackson for an episode of Urban

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.749
Myths led to immediate backlash.

00:00:20.749 --> 00:00:24.939
It was another groan-worthy installment of
the Hollywood whitewashing tradition that

00:00:24.939 --> 00:00:28.949
seemed like blatant disrespect towards the
former King of Pop.

00:00:28.949 --> 00:00:32.930
Following the backlash, the network decided
to pull the episode, writing,

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:37.910
"This decision was taken in light of the concerns
expressed by Michael Jackson's immediate family.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:42.410
We set out to take a light-hearted look at
reportedly true events [and] never intended

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.160
to cause any offence.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.400
Joseph Fiennes fully supports our decision."

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.700
Keanu Reeves has quite a few performances
to his name that just make you say,

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.340
"Whoa."

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.870
The one that takes the cake, though, is his
supporting role as Jonathan Harker in Bram

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.740
Stoker's Dracula.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:03.980
Despite the fact that the film won three Oscars
for its costuming, sound effects, and makeup

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:09.380
crews, Reeves' portrayal was marred by a terrible
British accent and over-the-top reactions.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:13.420
"Doctor, you must understand.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.240
I doubted everything, even my mind."

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.179
Director Francis Ford Coppola kindly remarked
that Reeves tried hard when it came to speaking

00:01:23.179 --> 00:01:27.899
with an English affectation, but that so much
effort was ultimately the issue with his portrayal,

00:01:27.899 --> 00:01:28.899
saying,

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:32.700
"He wanted to do it perfectly and in trying
to do it perfectly it came off as stilted."

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.340
M. Night Shyamalan was on a real cold streak
by the time he decided to helm a live-action

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:42.039
adaptation of the animated series Avatar:
The Last Airbender.

00:01:42.039 --> 00:01:45.749
Unfortunately, the movie flopped both critically
and at the box office.

00:01:45.749 --> 00:01:51.090
Part of the blame for the box office bomb
has to go to Shyamalan casting white actors,

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.840
such as Jackson Rathbone and Nicola Peltz,
in Asian roles.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:59.999
As a result of his role-casting decisions,
the film was met with wide "racebending" protests

00:01:59.999 --> 00:02:04.399
that called into question why the filmmaker
didn't opt for a more culturally representative

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.400
set of actors.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:10.760
Arguably the biggest problem in Spider-Man
3 is the character of Eddie Brock, a.k.a.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:11.760
Venom.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.440
When the movie was first announced, fans were
psyched to see who Sony would cast for the

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:20.040
role of the popular Spider-Man villain, but
somehow Topher Grace nabbed the role.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.520
"Look, I wanna kill the spider, you wanna
kill the spider.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:28.200
Together, he doesn't stand a chance.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.780
Interested?"

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:34.260
In the comics, Eddie Brock is a physically
imposing guy; Topher Grace, on the other hand,

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.510
isn't exactly Mr. Universe.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:39.880
Even the actor himself was baffled when he
was offered the gig.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:45.120
Speaking on an episode of the Inside of You
podcast, Grace said he was a huge fan of the

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.550
character, and sees Tom Hardy's portrayal
as a more accurate version.

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:52.520
"I was surprised and a little bit like 'huh'
when they wanted me to play it, so when I

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:56.140
look at it now, at the movie that's coming
out, I go, 'That's the guy.'"

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:02.920
In Prometheus, Guy Pearce plays Peter Weyland,
the ancient and affluent CEO of the villainous

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:04.580
Weyland Corporation.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:08.950
Weyland is hoping to find something out in
space that will help him beat death.

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.020
One look at his face and we can see why.

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:16.460
The horrible prosthetics are incredibly distracting,
and despite his acting chops, Pearce is never

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.450
convincing as an old man.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:23.070
Pearce later explained there was in fact supposed
to be a dream sequence showing Weyland as

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:27.920
a younger man, which was the sole reason he
was cast instead of an elderly actor.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:32.580
Director Ridley Scott decided to scrap the
scene and keep Pearce and his unsightly prosthetics

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:33.240
anyway.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:37.960
When it comes to directing, M. Night Shyamalan
either strikes out hard or knocks the ball

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:38.970
out of the park.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:43.080
But when it comes to Shyamalan's acting, the
only times his performances work are when

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:46.400
he relegates himself to a Hitchcock-style
cameo.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.720
When he actually tries to act, you wish he'd
spend all his time behind the camera.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.790
That's especially true in Lady in the Water.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.180
Shyamalan's character, Vick Ran, is crucial
to the plot.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:01.790
And unfortunately, he's stiff and dry, a cardboard
cutout come to life.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:06.220
The whole thing is especially embarrassing
because Shyamalan, who writes his own screenplays,

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:10.460
plays an author who is writing a book so important
that it's going to change the course of human

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:11.490
events.

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:12.480
What an ego.

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:18.880
Working with director Bong Joon-ho, Jake Gyllenhaal
starred as Dr. Johnny Wilcox in the 2017 film

00:04:18.881 --> 00:04:19.930
Okja.

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:25.010
The story follows a young Korean girl named
Mija as she tries to rescue her best friend,

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:30.460
a genetically modified super pig named Okja,
from an all-powerful American corporation

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:32.880
that wants to turn her into pork chops.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:38.790
And in her quest to rescue Okja, Mija runs
across Dr. Johnny, a shrill TV host who spends

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:42.290
his time screaming, sobbing, and acting like
a sadist.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:46.630
While Dr. Johnny could've been an interesting
character and a fun bad guy, Gyllenhaal's

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:49.200
instincts here are just all wrong.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:52.310
He hits the highest decibel possible with
every single line.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:05:00.360
"She is an amazing little lady, and she happens
to be the brain behind this entire super-pig

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:01.360
project!"

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:05.940
He squeals and whines, and there's never a
moment where we see Dr. Johnny as anything

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.270
other than a clown.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:13.190
Bong Joon-ho movies generally excel at giving
graceful and powerful moments to oddball characters,

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:17.660
but Gyllenhaal is so loud and so overwhelming
that not even his awesome mustache can make

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.320
for those over-the-top antics.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:25.420
In the year 2017, you'd think Hollywood would
finally realize that casting culturally appropriate

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:26.600
actors is a good idea.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:31.870
But evidently, the folks at Lionsgate missed
the memo when casting their Hellboy reboot.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:36.150
Everybody was happy when David Harbour signed
up to play the big red half-demon, but the

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:41.490
internet lost its collective mind when Ed
Skrein was tapped to star as Major Ben Daimio.

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:47.580
If you're not familiar with Hellboy lore,
Ben Daimio is a member of the BPRD and a U.S.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:51.680
Marine who came back to life after a rescue
mission gone wrong.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.800
He's also Japanese-American.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:57.450
Ed Skrein of Deadpool fame, on the other hand,
is very much a white dude.

00:05:57.450 --> 00:06:02.090
So naturally, some people were pretty upset
about the news, and the online furor prompted

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.250
Skrein to step down from the part.

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:08.750
He described his decision to leave the project
as "the right thing to do and the only thing

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:14.170
to do," and Lionsgate rectified their mistake
by recasting Daimio with Daniel Dae Kim.

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:19.070
Granted, Kim is Korean-American and not Japanese,
but that's still better than casting a white

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:21.650
guy best known for playing villains with British
accents.

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:28.080
"My welcome speech used to be full of euphemisms
like 'this may hurt a little' and 'this may

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.080
cause you some discomfort.'"

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:36.340
Directed by David Ayer, Suicide Squad is maybe
the most controversial DCEU movie to date.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:40.160
Maybe that's because it underwent some major
reshoots, or maybe it's because there were

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.730
just far too many characters in one film.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:47.110
In fact, there were so many bad guys running
around that one particular villain got very

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:50.330
little time in the spotlight: the Joker.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:55.280
Jared Leto isn't a horrible Joker, but he
doesn't really add anything to the role either.

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:59.940
The Clown Prince of Crime is the most iconic
villain in comic book history, and you really

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:02.320
need a special actor to bring him to life.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:07.020
But Leto relies too much on his flashy grill
and psycho eccentricities.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:11.870
He snarls and grimaces and does a kooky laugh,
but you never feel the monster brimming under

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:13.139
all that makeup.

00:07:13.139 --> 00:07:17.010
"I am not someone who is loved.

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:18.669
I'm an idea.

00:07:18.669 --> 00:07:21.760
A state of mind."

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:28.100
On August 21st, 2015, three American friends
stopped a heavily armed psycho on a train

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.020
heading from Amsterdam to Paris.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:35.500
The friends were Spencer Stone, Alek Skarlatos,
and Anthony Sadler, and together they took

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:39.100
the alleged terrorist down and saved everyone
on the train.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:43.600
Their story of bravery made quite an impression
on director Clint Eastwood, who turned the

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:45.830
story into a motion picture.

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:49.710
Only instead of hiring professional actors
to play the three leads, he decided to cast

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:53.290
the actual guys who were aboard the train
that fateful day.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:57.550
Obviously, these three men were incredibly
courageous, but being a real-life hero doesn't

00:07:57.550 --> 00:07:58.930
mean you can play one.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:03.020
When The 15:17 to Paris pulled into movie
theaters, critics paid their respects to the

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:07.360
trio's heroism but had to admit that none
of these dudes were going to be the next Daniel

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:08.360
Day-Lewis.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:11.870
It was a bold move by Eastwood to give these
guys a chance at movie stardom, but by the

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:15.540
end of the film, it's very apparent why big-time
actors make the big bucks.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:20.800
Over 30 years after getting turned into a
big game trophy in the original, Shane Black

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.949
returned to the world of Predator in 2018.

00:08:23.949 --> 00:08:28.790
Only this time, he was behind the camera and
directing a cast that included Olivia Munn,

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:32.580
Jacob Tremblay, Sterling K. Brown, and Keegan-Michael
Key.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:37.200
In addition to those big names, Black hired
one of his good friends for a small role.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:42.011
Steven Wilder Striegel had known Black for
years: In fact, he appeared in some of the

00:08:42.011 --> 00:08:46.010
director's earlier films, like Iron Man 3
and The Nice Guys.

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:49.570
Striegel was to play an annoying jogger who
hits on Olivia Munn's character in a brief

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:51.420
scene in The Predator.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:52.790
And then this happened.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:57.051
"A scene was taken out of the new Predator
film after a last-minute revelation that one

00:08:57.051 --> 00:09:00.649
of the actor's involved is a convicted sex
offender."

00:09:00.649 --> 00:09:06.260
When Munn discovered her co-star's background,
she told 20th Century Fox, and the studio

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:08.080
cut Striegel's scene out of the movie.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:14.500
Irish actor Colin Farrell has had a fair number
of acclaim-worthy performances, but his eponymous

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:17.020
turn in Alexander was not one of them.

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:21.670
Not only has his casting been panned because
he's not, you know, Greek, but he wasn't convincing

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:23.790
as the amoral emperor either.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:28.480
Farrell, for his part, has since been able
to laugh off the criticism, particularly when

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:31.190
it comes to his terrible bleach blonde locks.

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:35.490
He gave an interview on The Graham Norton
Show in 2013 where he suggested some retroactive

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:36.490
changes :

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:37.490
"He should've been brunette.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:38.490
For sure.

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:45.340
And maybe he shouldn't have had an Irish accent,
only from the 7,000 reviews I read."

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:50.600
Even George Clooney knows that his casting
as Bruce Wayne was all wrong, almost as wrong

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:54.180
as the entirety of 1997's Batman &amp; Robin.

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:58.450
As Clooney recalled in a hilarious interview
with The Graham Norton Show, he doesn't mind

00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.980
apologizing for the role:

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:03.380
"I always apologize for Batman and Robin.

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:07.120
I thought at the time, 'This is going to be
a very good career move.'

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.120
Um…

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:09.780
It wasn't."

